  "limitations": [
    "For SCHED-02, occurrence means the exact due instant already persisted as next_run_at_utc. SCHED-03 owns durable occurrence IDs and rows, uniqueness, and Work and Run ingress.",
    "An exclusive active lease is not exactly-once processing. The owner, due instant, and claimed version form a fencing tuple for later processing and release operations.",
    "Strictly expired leases are mechanically reclaimable here. SCHED-06 retains restart recovery and proof that reclaiming an expired lease cannot duplicate occurrence or work creation.",
    "SCHED-04 retains grace and skip or run_once misfire behavior. SCHED-05 retains recurrence recomputation, occurrence, work, audit, next-time advancement, and lease release in one transaction.",
    "Runtime concurrency is exercised with independent sessions on file-backed SQLite. PostgreSQL table and constraint DDL compile, but PostgreSQL runtime contention is not executed.",
    "The consistency digest detects unrecomputed drift but is unkeyed. Worker polling, renewal, processing, audit, metrics, APIs, authorization, migrations, and live deployment remain later requirements."
  ]
